== Data Structure Overview ==
'''Scribunto''' module (database) for storing and configuring all possible entries (objects) used by:
* [[Template:Obj]] (combines color and icon with extra logic)
* [[Template:Color]] (color/classes-related text and link parameters)
* [[Template:I]] (icon parameter)

An object's existence within this module is required for it to work with the templates above (for organizational and other purposes).

To add color styling, visit [[Template:Color/styles.css]].

To add an entry to the database, enter editing mode and add the following entry to the appropriate location within the table (look for comments, which start with <code>--</code>):

<syntaxhighlight lang=lua>
["<Entry> (object name)"] = {
	["<Parameter (key)>"] = "<Value>",
	...
},
</syntaxhighlight>

<Parameter> can be one or more of the following:<br>
<small>(ONLY PROVIDE A VALUE IF IT IS REQUIRED FOR THE OBJECT)</small>

* <code>icon = <string>/false</code>
** Replaces default <code><Entry>.png</code> to the desired media.
** Set to '''false''' if the object is not intended to include media.
* <code>link = <string>/false</code>
** Replaces the default object hyperlink (which uses the object's name) with the specified string.
** Set to '''false''' to disable the hyperlink.
* <code>plural = <string></code>
** Provides the plural form for the Obj template (see examples).
* <code>text = <string></code>
** Replaces the object's name with custom text by default.
*** Can be used for objects with identical names, unique symbols that cannot be typed using a standard US keyboard, or similar cases (e.g., Singularity (Layer) -> Singularity, Jalabono -> Jalaboño).
* <code>color = <string>/false</code>
** Applies (reuses) the color of the specified object for the entry (points to self by default).
*** Inherits its "extraClass" parameter and CSS variables.
** Set to '''false''' if the object is not supposed to have color styling.
* <code>extraClass = <string></code>
** If the color requires additional CSS classes, specify them in a space-separated string.